    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Substantial Mixed-Use City-Centre Investment. 25/26 Mary Street Little offers an excellent opportunity to acquire a prime mixed-use asset in an evolving Dublin city-centre location. The property combines an established commercial income with vacant residential accommodation and clear potential for future rental and capital growth.\r\n\r\nThe building is a substantial four-storey over basement mixed-use investment positioned in the heart of Dublin city centre, close to Capel Street and Mary Street. The property comprises two ground-floor retail units together with seven spacious apartments on the upper floors, arranged as 3 x three-bed, 2 x two-bed and 2 x one-bed apartments. The residential accommodation has independent access and is presented in good, tenantable condition. However, being sold with vacant possession offers a significant opportunity to establish rents at current market level with some refurbishments. The retail tenants in situ since  2002 are paying  substantial rent with a lease in place until January 2030 providing a positive income stream in the short to medium term. Viewing is highly recommended and strictly by prior appointment."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Retail: Large ground-floor retail unit fitted out as supermarket with basement storage area. approx. 190 sq.m ( excluding basement). \r\n\r\nEntrance hall: 6.9m x 1.20m  with storage and staircase to upper floors. \r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nLanding: 4.21m x 2.98m.\r\n\r\nApartment 1 — One bedroom — 31 sq. m\r\nEntrance hall, kitchen / living room, shower room and bedroom.\r\n\r\nApartment 2 — Two bedrooms — 48 sq. m\r\nEntrance hall, shower room, kitchen / dining room and two bedrooms.\r\n\r\nApartment 3 — Three bedrooms — 58 sq. m\r\nEntrance hall, shower room, kitchen / living room and three bedrooms. Terrace off the living room.\r\n\r\nSecond Floor\r\nLanding: 4.21m x 2.98m.\r\n\r\nApartment 4 — One bedroom — 31 sq. m\r\nEntrance hall, kitchen / living room, shower room and bedroom.\r\n\r\nApartment 5 — Two bedrooms — 48.6 sq. m\r\nEntrance hall, shower room, kitchen / living room and two bedrooms.\r\n\r\nApartment 6 — Three bedrooms — 61 sq. m\r\nEntrance hall, shower room, kitchen / living room and three bedrooms.\r\n\r\nThird Floor\r\nApartment 7 — Three bedrooms — 69 sq. m\r\nEntrance hall, shower room, kitchen / living room and three bedrooms."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Prime Dublin city-centre location\r\nSubstantial four-storey over basement mixed-use investment\r\nPinoy Sari Sari Ltd in situ since 2002 trading as specialist supermarket. \r\nApartments to be sold with vacant possession\r\nLarge apartments with value add potential\r\nWithin walking distance of Henry Street, O’Connell Street, Capel Street, Trinity College, the Four Courts, Smithfield and the Docklands"
      },
      {
